SUMMARY:Lec84|How Many Shots Does It Take? Rethinking Resource Allocation on Noisy Quantum Computers|Prateek P. Kulkarni-Indian Institute of Science (IISc)
LOCATION:https://tinyurl.com/gucs-zoom
DESCRIPTION:Quantum algorithms require repeated circuit executions\, or shots\, to obtain reliable results — but how many shots are actually enough? In this talk\, I will present our ISLPED 2026 work on noise-aware quantum resource allocation. We develop an analytical framework for estimating the shots required for reliable execution based on circuit and hardware characteristics\, and extend it to optimally allocate a fixed shot budget across circuit partitions.\n\nOn real quantum hardware\, our approach reduces required shots by about 58%\, energy consumption by up to 62%\, and estimation error by up to 73%. More broadly\, I will discuss why treating shots as a hardware-aware resource can make near-term quantum execution substantially more efficient.
URL:https://qucs.info/lectures/84-how-many-shots-does-it-take-rethinking-resource-allocation-on-noisy-quantum-computers
END:VEVENT
